<p>Thanks for the upvote. Glad you found it to be potent.</p>
<p>With respect to your comment on this being similar to other skips, I don't doubt it. Depression and mental health issues have been common themes in tales and articles across the site's history and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1538066782" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;">Ihp</a></span>'s <a href="/scp-3020">SCP-3020</a> is one of the more notable examples of this.</p>
<p>I'd argue that classifying this as Depression: The SCP Article is a bit of missing the forest for the trees, as ultimately this is not an article about depression as much as it is about a kind of toxic stoicism.</p>

