<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4560 infected individuals observed in private appear to retain the ability to express negative emotions to themselves, though unable to record these feelings through written or verbal means.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This really struck a chord with me. I get overwhelmed from time to time and I often turn to writing to just get all those confusing and distracting thoughts out of my head. I can't imagine what it would be like to not be able to do that, and that sort of thought stuck with me after I read the article.</p>
<p>Also, nice call on keeping the last note in a collapsible. Even though it's short enough to not really need it, I think it's a good move because it makes the reader open up that last bit to finish the story. The message itself gave me chills. Great way to end the piece.</p>
<p>Nicely done, Conwell!</p>

