<p>Thanks for breaking it down for me. You're right , I was missing the trick. I still am, but less so now.</p>
<p>If you haven't already heard enough from me, here's a few more of my thoughts:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">About&nbsp;the&nbsp;Dispatched&nbsp;MTF&nbsp;Squads</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Enough&nbsp;About&nbsp;the&nbsp;Dispatched&nbsp;MTF&nbsp;Squads</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I get it now. Upon first read, I didn't get the impression that containing the initial outbreak was a big deal, nor that those infected were particularly dangerous or contagious. So I initially thought having three squads felt like overkill.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">About&nbsp;Identifying&nbsp;as&nbsp;Male</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Enough&nbsp;About&nbsp;Gender&nbsp;Studies</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The phrase &quot;identifying as male&quot; and the idea that the SCP only affects men (stereotypically more emotionally repressed) makes me think of toxic masculinity. That military mindset of never complaining or showing weakness. I might be reaching, though.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">About&nbsp;the&nbsp;Note</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Enough&nbsp;About&nbsp;the&nbsp;Note</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It didn't even occur to me about his problems being pent up. That makes sense. An SCP that is the opposite of a therapist.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">About&nbsp;Stages&nbsp;of&nbsp;Infection</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Enough&nbsp;About&nbsp;the&nbsp;Infection</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I felt like I really wanted to see more examples, or an overview of, the infection at various stages. This could also have the added benefit of being more obvious as to why patient zero was driven to suicide in the first place (for those of us who maybe didn't pick up on that cough)</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Thanks for clearing it up. I'll go from -1 to neutral vote, since I better understand things now.</p>

							</div>

								
					
